From 0c0c83b27a6a49a0c740904c02886486fac37bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:28:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cast: Implement remote playback control requests

Cast routes advertise the MediaControlIntent remote playback actions
(PLAY, SEEK, GET_STATUS, PAUSE, RESUME, STOP and the session actions),
but the route controller rejected every control request, so apps using
RemotePlaybackClient could select a Cast route and then not play on it.

Handle them on the Default Media Receiver: PLAY attaches to (or
launches) CC1AD845 on the route's CastV2 session and sends LOAD on the
media namespace; the other actions map to SEEK, GET_STATUS, PAUSE, PLAY
and STOP on the loaded media session. One remote playback session with
one item is kept, like the Default Media Receiver plays one item.

- MEDIA_STATUS updates the item status, which is reported in the
  results and through the client's status update receivers, including
  the end of playback and the receiver app being stopped or replaced.
- Commands sent while the item is still launching or loading are
  applied once the LOAD reply arrives.
- Ending a session stops the receiver application; a PLAY that follows
  before the stop is confirmed launches it again instead of attaching to
  the instance that is going away. START_SESSION stops the media of the
  session it replaces.
- "Stop casting" (UNSELECT_REASON_STOPPED) stops the receiver
  application remote playback runs on.
- If the route's connection dropped while it stays selected, a new
  request opens it again.
